  "raw": " Even individuals that long have a deeper sense of self that is present during life, lose it as they age; this phenomenon can be viewed if someone matures further than others around and dies before his or her fully mature years are reached. In this case aging preserves a capacity within people even after death. This adaptation provides what could be defined as knowledge but not raw logic.\nMany famous figures throughout history experience death early (some known for their insanity). Still many die peacefully of old age. As we can observe from early mammalian history we as humans possess an undercurrent of reckless, transcendental motive-driven behavior when coming into conflict with other animals; yet somehow this danger persists in ways that rivals to no end today. I believe this aspect truly existed at some point given early evolution and shows up particularly within patriarchal cultures - which has contributed significantly to our smaller advanced brain capacity in modern times. Patriarchal hierarchy presenting female dominance over males does cause scripture for sure and even shows hypersexualize mainly females then",
